    howToBecome: `Путь в Product Design почти всегда начинается с UX/UI Design experience — очень редко можно стать Product Designer напрямую без design baseline. Realistic timeline: 2-4 года как UX/UI Designer plus 6-18 месяцев conscious transition к product thinking.

Prerequisite Strong UX/UI Foundation (2-4 года): Сначала станьте competent UX/UI Designer: владейте Figma на advanced level, создавайте pixel-perfect mockups, понимайте design principles, проводите basic user research и usability testing. Build portfolio из 3-5 сильных UX/UI projects. Это baseline — без design craft невозможно стать Product Designer. Если вы уже UX/UI Designer с 2 plus годами experience, ready для transition.

Develop Product Thinking (6-12 месяцев интенсивного learning): Ключевое отличие Product Designer от UX/UI — product mindset. Изучите: (1) Product Management fundamentals — прочитайте "Inspired" by Marty Cagan (bible of product management, 2 недели), "The Lean Startup" by Eric Ries, "Hooked" by Nir Eyal. (2) Business metrics — understand key metrics: DAU/MAU (daily/monthly active users), retention (D1/D7/D30 retention curves), conversion rates, churn, LTV (lifetime value), CAC (customer acquisition cost). Learn как design влияет на эти metrics. (3) Jobs To Be Done framework — Clayton Christensen methodology для understanding user motivations (better чем personas). (4) Prioritization frameworks — RICE (Reach, Impact, Confidence, Effort), ICE scoring, Kano model.

Learn Analytics and A/B Testing (3-6 месяцев): Product Designer должен be comfortable с data. (1) Learn analytics tools: Amplitude (бесплатный scholarship program для learning), Mixpanel, Google Analytics 4. Изучите event tracking, funnels, cohort analysis, retention curves. (2) A/B testing basics — understand statistical significance (p-values, confidence intervals), sample size calculation, experiment design. Курсы: Udacity "A/B Testing" (free), Coursera "Experimentation for Improvement". (3) SQL basics — ability to write simple queries для pulling data (не обязательно, но highly valuable). Codecademy "Learn SQL" (2-3 недели).

Transition Strategy в текущей компании (наиболее реалистичный путь): Если вы already UX/UI Designer, easiest transition — evolve роль внутри текущей компании: (1) Start participating в product discussions — attend roadmap planning meetings (ask PM if you can join), contribute ideas proactively. (2) Propose metrics для tracking design impact — before designing feature, define success metrics (conversion rate, task completion time), track post-launch, present findings. (3) Conduct research proactively — don't wait for PM to request research, initiate user interviews yourself, bring insights к team. (4) Partner closely с PM — schedule weekly syncs, ask questions about business context, offer design perspective на product decisions early. (5) After 6-12 months demonstrating product thinking, talk to manager о role transition — "I've been working more like Product Designer (metrics, strategy, research ownership), can we formalize this?"

Alternative Apply для Product Designer roles externally: Если internal transition не работает, apply directly для Product Designer positions (требуется 2-4 года UX/UI experience baseline). Ключевые моменты в portfolio и interviews: (1) Reframe case studies — показывайте не только design process, но product context: business goals, metrics impact ("redesign increased conversion from 8% to 11.5%"), how you collaborated с PM/Engineering, trade-offs и decisions. (2) Demonstrate product thinking в interviews — when asked "design a feature", start с questions: "What's the business goal?", "What metrics matter?", "Who are the users?". Show strategic thinking, not just visual design. (3) Prepare for product questions — interviewers will ask product-style questions: "How would you prioritize features X, Y, Z?", "What metrics would you track?". Practice frameworks (RICE, Jobs To Be Done).

Courses и Resources: (1) Reforge "Product Design" course ($2000, 6 недель, gold standard для transitioning к Product Design — covers product thinking, metrics, A/B testing). (2) Interaction Design Foundation "Design Thinking", "Data-Driven Design" (subscription $16/month). (3) Books: "Inspired" by Marty Cagan, "Trustworthy Online Controlled Experiments" by Kohavi et al. (A/B testing bible), "The Design of Everyday Things" by Don Norman. (4) Podcasts: "Lenny's Podcast" (product management, часто design topics), "Design Better Podcast" by InVision.

Portfolio Requirements для Product Designer roles: 3-4 case studies showing: (1) Business context upfront — what was product goal, business metric targeted. (2) Research and discovery — how you identified problem (user interviews, analytics data). (3) Design process — ideation, iterations, prototyping. (4) Validation — usability testing, A/B tests. (5) Impact measurement — post-launch metrics, what changed, what you learned. Avoid pure visual showcases — companies хотят видеть product thinking, not just pretty pixels.

Timeline: 2-4 года UX/UI baseline plus 6-12 месяцев focused transition (learning product thinking, analytics, building product-focused portfolio) plus 3-6 месяцев job search. Total 3-5 лет от начала design career к Product Designer роли. Fast-track possible если вы quick learner в strong product company (18-24 месяца в некоторых cases).`,
